WEBVTT

01:30.520 --> 01:32.940
Episode 3: Humpty Dumpty

01:32.940 --> 01:35.940
Midterms

01:32.940 --> 01:35.940
Period 1: Biology

01:32.940 --> 01:35.940
Period 2: Classic Literature

01:48.310 --> 01:50.390
Hey! Stay focused!

01:54.880 --> 01:58.130
<b>Kobato Japanese Confectionery</b>

02:01.330 --> 02:04.310
<i>Kobato-kun? It's me, Osanai.</i>

02:04.310 --> 02:07.470
Huh? You don't call often. What's up?

02:07.470 --> 02:10.630
<i>Listen, could I see you for a bit?</i>

02:11.020 --> 02:12.840
Sure. Where?

02:17.410 --> 02:19.440
Humpty Dumpty.

02:19.440 --> 02:24.300
Humpty Dumpty? I thought you said
 you were staying away from there.

02:24.300 --> 02:25.390
<i>Don't say that.</i>

02:26.150 --> 02:27.910
<i>Don't say anything.</i>

02:28.520 --> 02:29.600
All right.

02:33.020 --> 02:36.120
Is Osanai-san going to stress eat again?

02:38.270 --> 02:40.170
Are you laughing to yourself?

02:40.170 --> 02:41.600
When did you get here?

02:42.030 --> 02:43.300
Just now.

02:43.300 --> 02:46.780
Oh, you bought a new bike, huh?

02:46.780 --> 02:47.560
Yeah.

02:48.120 --> 02:48.940
Let's go.

02:50.810 --> 02:53.310
<b>All You Can Eat Cakes</b>

02:50.810 --> 02:53.310
<b>Adults</b>

02:50.810 --> 02:53.310
<b>Children</b>

02:51.400 --> 02:55.080
I'll have a standard 
chiffon cake and a coffee.

02:55.080 --> 03:00.950
Also, the mille-feuille, the panna cotta, 
and the strawberry shortcake.

03:03.790 --> 03:06.110
I'll just start with a coffee.

03:06.110 --> 03:09.050
Oh, and a Mont Blanc.

03:09.870 --> 03:10.970
Just the one.

03:16.930 --> 03:18.100
Is something wrong?

03:18.460 --> 03:19.680
Nothing.

03:25.330 --> 03:26.600
How'd the exams go?

03:29.420 --> 03:32.730
Yeah, I did all right, I guess.

03:32.730 --> 03:35.360
Yeah? Glad to hear it.

03:35.870 --> 03:36.980
But...

03:39.640 --> 03:41.860
I kinda messed up in biology.

03:42.390 --> 03:46.580
The enzymes that convert peptone 
and protein into polypeptides...

03:46.580 --> 03:52.510
I got peptidase first, 
but I couldn't think of any more.

03:53.910 --> 03:56.660
And I was so sure I knew them.

03:57.780 --> 03:59.250
But...

03:59.250 --> 04:00.400
That's when...

04:01.830 --> 04:03.580
I heard some glass shatter.

04:03.580 --> 04:04.690
Uh-huh.

04:05.230 --> 04:07.840
From the cleaning cupboard in class.

04:07.840 --> 04:09.650
A vase smashed loudly.

04:11.440 --> 04:14.870
And I clean forgot everything.

04:15.850 --> 04:19.530
It was a lot of work cleaning up
 the water that had spilled.

04:19.530 --> 04:21.850
That must have been rough.

04:27.000 --> 04:30.660
And I got kind of sad.

04:31.050 --> 04:32.410
Sad?

04:32.410 --> 04:34.630
And I was looking for you.

04:34.630 --> 04:38.320
Have you been looking for me 
since the exams ended?

04:38.740 --> 04:39.740
Yeah.

04:39.740 --> 04:42.430
You could've just texted me.

04:42.430 --> 04:44.050
I did.

04:44.050 --> 04:45.840
Not that you replied.

04:51.280 --> 04:52.900
My phone's at school.

04:52.900 --> 04:54.070
It is?

04:54.070 --> 04:55.210
Yeah.

04:55.210 --> 04:58.810
I forgot I turned it off before 
the exams and left it in my locker.

04:59.400 --> 05:00.810
Wanna go get it?

05:05.300 --> 05:08.190
Yeah. I think I'll go get it.

05:08.580 --> 05:10.260
I think you should.

05:21.460 --> 05:26.470
Do you have time after?

05:22.460 --> 05:26.470
Let's go get cake

05:23.460 --> 05:26.470
Where are you?

05:24.470 --> 05:26.470
Looks like your phone's off

05:25.470 --> 05:26.470
Kobato-kun?

05:26.470 --> 05:28.290
I feel bad for missing her messages.

05:30.280 --> 05:33.470
Now... Better finish the errand I was sent on.

05:34.590 --> 05:38.970
A vase smashed in the cleaning 
cupboard during the exams?

05:39.500 --> 05:42.060
Someone must have rigged it.

05:45.430 --> 05:47.350
Pardon me.

06:10.890 --> 06:13.890
Are you still at Humpty Dumpty?

06:12.390 --> 06:13.890
I'm working on a pumpkin pudding

06:14.140 --> 06:15.270
I'm back.

06:21.220 --> 06:22.530
Can you finish all that?

06:24.670 --> 06:28.420
I wanted the marjolaine, 
but I don't think I can.

06:30.980 --> 06:32.090
Well?

06:39.610 --> 06:41.350
I'm sorry!

06:42.660 --> 06:44.550
Yeah, you'd definitely look.

06:45.180 --> 06:50.000
Everyone turns to look 
whenever there's a loud sound.

06:50.000 --> 06:52.430
It's a natural instinct for any being.

06:52.840 --> 06:57.510
Even if it's during an exam, 
when you're not allowed to look around.

07:11.530 --> 07:15.280
amylase amylum

07:11.530 --> 07:15.280
--> maltose

07:11.530 --> 07:15.280
maltase maltose

07:11.530 --> 07:15.280
--> glucose

07:11.530 --> 07:15.280
sucrase sucrose

07:11.530 --> 07:15.280
--> glucose

07:11.530 --> 07:15.280
+ fructose

07:11.530 --> 07:15.280
trypsin protein peptin

07:11.530 --> 07:15.280
--> polypeptides

07:21.290 --> 07:23.430
Or so my friend tells me.

07:24.140 --> 07:25.180
Which desk?

07:25.180 --> 07:30.420
A decent, ordinary man would surely keep that
a secret, especially after ripping off the tape.

07:31.640 --> 07:35.810
They must have been really careless 
if they forgot to remove the evidence.

07:36.170 --> 07:37.400
I'm not sure.

07:38.040 --> 07:43.700
Hard to imagine that someone clever enough 
to rig that vase to smash would be so lax.

07:45.220 --> 07:49.620
The situation may have 
been more complicated.

07:50.010 --> 07:52.690
They wanted someone else
 to take the blame?

07:53.000 --> 07:55.390
I'm not sure what the truth is.

07:57.620 --> 07:59.700
Either way, it doesn't matter now.

07:59.700 --> 08:02.170
A broken vase won't fix itself.

08:02.710 --> 08:04.950
Would you like some more coffee?

08:06.010 --> 08:08.920
Plus, a marjolaine and a savarin.

08:09.340 --> 08:12.840
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

08:09.340 --> 08:12.840
<b>Kira West
Driving School</b>

08:10.460 --> 08:12.190
I'm surprised you resisted.

08:13.140 --> 08:15.210
It's no big deal.

08:15.210 --> 08:20.140
An ordinary person shouldn't get upset
 over an exam question or two.

08:20.140 --> 08:23.620
Reviewing questions
 is out of the question.

08:24.090 --> 08:24.940
Yeah.

08:25.850 --> 08:27.930
Today was a good day.

08:27.930 --> 08:31.130
Exams are over, and I had cake.

08:34.600 --> 08:35.910
Sakagami!

08:37.510 --> 08:39.160
Don't, Osanai-san!

08:51.100 --> 08:53.010
You won't catch up to him.

08:53.010 --> 08:55.010
Let's go home, Osanai-san.

09:06.800 --> 09:08.320
Kobato-kun.

09:08.320 --> 09:10.240
I saw you going in.

09:12.200 --> 09:14.890
That's your second time 
being summoned, huh?

09:15.630 --> 09:21.630
The first was when your bike was 
spotted at the scene of a theft, wasn't it?

09:22.150 --> 09:23.030
Yeah.

09:26.510 --> 09:31.430
A student named Iokibe 
lives in an apartment in Hondo-cho.

09:31.430 --> 09:32.580
Iokibe?

09:33.080 --> 09:36.680
It's written with the kanji for 
"five hundred" and "flag bearer."

09:37.850 --> 09:43.140
Their stamp and ID documents were stolen 
while they were at the ballot box.

09:44.090 --> 09:46.020
How do you know all that?

09:46.470 --> 09:49.270
I got upset and looked them up.

09:50.740 --> 09:52.770
So what was it about today?

09:55.210 --> 09:57.490
They found my bike.

10:00.940 --> 10:07.220
A car ran over it last night, and that person
 called the school to complain?

10:09.740 --> 10:14.300
They have some nerve, complaining after 
running over it due to their own carelessness.

10:16.440 --> 10:18.500
Poor driver.

10:19.860 --> 10:23.910
They must not have been expecting
to drive over a bike here.

10:24.330 --> 10:26.070
T-True.

10:26.530 --> 10:29.070
It's all Sakagami's fault.

10:30.610 --> 10:33.810
Sakagami probably stepped on this part.

10:42.840 --> 10:43.980
Kobato-kun.

10:44.980 --> 10:47.310
What do you think happened yesterday?

10:48.940 --> 10:50.320
Well...

10:52.020 --> 10:53.720
Um...

11:00.220 --> 11:03.600
All right. I think it went
 something like this.

11:40.900 --> 11:43.310
And he ran off.

11:43.310 --> 11:44.430
Where to?

11:47.730 --> 11:51.500
What business could he possibly have
here on the outskirts of town?

11:52.370 --> 11:54.430
Stay calm, Osanai-san.

11:55.060 --> 11:57.450
I'm calm.

11:59.060 --> 12:02.460
Sakagami was wearing 
a Minakami High School uniform, right?

12:02.940 --> 12:07.300
Some of the people we saw at 
the convenience store were on bikes.

12:07.680 --> 12:11.720
Assuming they bike to school, 
they might live around here somewhere.

12:12.330 --> 12:14.890
Their group seems to have a pecking order.

12:14.890 --> 12:17.920
Maybe he was hurrying 
to get to his senpai's place.

12:18.280 --> 12:21.720
Even if that's true, 
how would he have gotten home?

12:22.220 --> 12:26.560
He wouldn't have had a reason to hurry 
home. He could've just taken the bus.

12:26.560 --> 12:29.090
Or someone could've 
taken him home on their bike.

12:29.090 --> 12:32.540
But there are no bus stops around here.

12:33.410 --> 12:37.380
And he doesn't seem 
well-off enough to take a taxi.

12:39.460 --> 12:43.490
Maybe this wasn't his destination.

12:44.030 --> 12:46.950
The left road would've
taken him back into the city.

12:46.950 --> 12:50.110
He wouldn't have had 
any reason to go over the hill.

12:50.650 --> 12:53.970
That would mean he'd go right.

12:55.430 --> 12:57.760
Sakagami got around on a bicycle...

12:58.540 --> 13:03.480
And he stole Osanai-san's bicycle 
because his got stolen.

13:03.480 --> 13:08.510
Some people in his group 
used bikes to get around.

13:08.770 --> 13:12.030
It looks like there's 
a driving school up ahead.

13:13.040 --> 13:17.030
Sakagami might have been trying 
to get his motorcycle license.

13:19.600 --> 13:23.950
But we passed a driving school 
on the way here, didn't we?

13:22.030 --> 13:24.400
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

13:22.030 --> 13:24.400
<b>Kira West
Driving School</b>

13:25.010 --> 13:26.210
That's true.

13:26.610 --> 13:31.370
Either way, we won't get any definitive 
answers based on the info we have now.

13:32.090 --> 13:36.960
I know it's maddening, 
but at least your bike turned up.

13:37.860 --> 13:39.160
Let's head home.

13:39.620 --> 13:42.070
I'm not mad.

13:43.310 --> 13:45.660
I'm going to stay here a little longer.

13:45.660 --> 13:46.960
What for?

13:48.130 --> 13:52.380
It's almost the same time 
we saw Sakagami yesterday.

14:12.610 --> 14:13.960
Kobato-kun, look.

14:16.790 --> 14:19.710
<b>Kira North Driving School</b>

14:22.680 --> 14:23.820
I see.

14:24.220 --> 14:28.650
Sakagami must have missed 
 the driving school bus yesterday.

14:29.030 --> 14:33.460
So he sped on the bicycle and tried 
to get ahead of it by going over the hill.

14:34.220 --> 14:38.380
A free pickup bus would make stops 
even where there aren't bus stops.

14:38.380 --> 14:40.600
And it would have a fixed schedule.

14:41.120 --> 14:43.100
He'd have no trouble getting home, too.

14:44.610 --> 14:48.450
Which is why he threw away 
the bike he stole from me.

14:48.990 --> 14:51.030
Now that we've seen the bus, too,

14:51.030 --> 14:54.970
we can say for sure that he was 
trying to get to the driving school.

14:55.800 --> 14:58.690
Why don't we call it quits and go?

15:00.210 --> 15:01.830
Call it quits?

15:03.330 --> 15:07.340
No. We're just getting started, Kobato-kun.

15:07.940 --> 15:10.140
We finally caught him.

15:10.580 --> 15:11.780
"Caught" him?

15:14.120 --> 15:19.020
He ruined my spring exclusive 
strawberry tarts.

15:20.130 --> 15:23.910
He threw my bicycle away
when he had no more use for it.

15:23.910 --> 15:31.350
I was hoping for a peaceful school life,
 but I've already been treated like a thief.

15:31.800 --> 15:34.280
The guidance counselor 
has summoned me twice.

15:35.370 --> 15:37.590
Well, Kobato-kun?

15:38.170 --> 15:39.950
What do you think of that?

15:41.170 --> 15:42.350
Osanai-san.

15:45.040 --> 15:47.070
I need to make him pay.

15:49.560 --> 15:51.320
Don't say that, Osanai-san.

15:51.320 --> 15:53.410
You got your bicycle back.

15:53.410 --> 15:54.930
You ought to be satisfied.

15:54.930 --> 15:58.590
Don't think about it any further. Let it go.

15:58.590 --> 16:01.110
We promised we'd be ordinary.

16:01.720 --> 16:05.480
We won't be ordinary people 
if we don't just let these things happen.

16:08.520 --> 16:09.810
But I...

16:09.810 --> 16:11.340
You have to resist.

16:11.340 --> 16:13.410
This is a test.

16:14.640 --> 16:16.420
But I...

16:17.840 --> 16:19.500
I didn't do anything.

16:20.490 --> 16:21.510
Nothing.

16:22.640 --> 16:23.880
And yet...

16:27.950 --> 16:31.060
Okay, Kobato-kun. How about this?

16:32.450 --> 16:33.570
How about what?

16:34.660 --> 16:39.990
What do you think is the most 
important thing to us ordinary people?

16:41.050 --> 16:43.360
Being content with what we have.

16:44.030 --> 16:47.870
Why don't we say that the most 
important thing to ordinary people...

16:50.570 --> 16:54.260
is making sure we continue
 to have what he have?

17:02.500 --> 17:07.750
Requesting backup in light of our need
 for additional mobile defense

17:06.000 --> 17:07.750
Dummy

17:08.280 --> 17:10.300
Hurry up and state your request.

17:10.300 --> 17:12.620
I'm going back to my club 
if it isn't worth my time.

17:12.950 --> 17:15.470
I think it's worthwhile.

17:15.470 --> 17:17.390
But it's also not quick to explain.

17:17.920 --> 17:20.030
Anyway, take a seat.

17:28.020 --> 17:30.150
I'm glad, though.

17:30.560 --> 17:34.410
You rarely hear of stolen bicycles turning up.

17:34.840 --> 17:38.280
You wouldn't have called me here
if you were <i>just</i> glad.

17:40.520 --> 17:44.290
Osanai-san intends to 
get revenge on the bicycle thief.

17:48.050 --> 17:49.470
Amazing.

17:49.470 --> 17:54.290
Teach that little punk 
what it means to steal from others.

17:54.580 --> 17:57.360
I'm sure <i>you</i> could teach him, Kengo.

17:57.360 --> 17:59.710
Your fists would do the talking,
 if it came to it.

18:00.250 --> 18:02.180
But we're talking about Osanai-san.

18:04.020 --> 18:08.440
You aren't asking me to be 
her bodyguard, are you?

18:08.440 --> 18:11.290
That's the basic idea.

18:11.700 --> 18:14.380
Is this a request from Osanai?

18:14.380 --> 18:15.170
No.

18:15.170 --> 18:17.150
Then, it's not my place to get involved.

18:17.150 --> 18:20.080
But Osanai-san's in danger.

18:20.430 --> 18:21.830
What danger?

18:21.830 --> 18:23.060
Well...

18:23.760 --> 18:25.370
Um...

18:25.880 --> 18:27.020
What's wrong?

18:27.430 --> 18:28.320
Oh, nothing.

18:33.320 --> 18:35.960
If you have something to tell me, say it.

18:36.810 --> 18:40.630
To be honest, 
I still haven't figured it all out.

18:41.150 --> 18:44.100
Then, get your "figuring out" done first.

18:47.610 --> 18:49.130
I don't get it.

18:49.600 --> 18:51.820
You have something in mind, don't you?

18:51.820 --> 18:53.960
And you're sure you can figure it out.

18:53.960 --> 18:55.300
So why don't you?

18:55.760 --> 18:58.850
Isn't this the kind of 
situation you thrive in?

18:59.410 --> 19:01.540
I used to.

19:02.780 --> 19:06.880
I don't like these situations anymore.

19:07.510 --> 19:14.970
I realized inserting myself into problems
 that people are working really hard on,

19:14.970 --> 19:18.720
then proceeding to solve them
 isn't really welcomed.

19:19.090 --> 19:22.560
Even fewer people thank me for it.

19:23.990 --> 19:29.430
I'm far more likely to be 
shunned and despised for it.

19:29.430 --> 19:31.200
That's not true.

19:31.200 --> 19:33.690
You might not understand.

19:33.690 --> 19:39.190
I've been seeing the truth of every situation 
before everyone else since elementary school.

19:39.820 --> 19:43.180
I'm done getting involved 
and being despised for it.

19:44.190 --> 19:48.450
I'm trying to be a modest, upright, ordinary 
person who's satisfied with the status quo!

19:48.450 --> 19:49.840
What's wrong with that?!

19:53.790 --> 19:56.170
Anyway, that's the gist of it.

19:56.170 --> 19:58.610
Is that good enough?

19:58.610 --> 20:00.090
In that case,

20:00.090 --> 20:02.370
all the more reason for you to think.

20:02.370 --> 20:04.080
That's more fitting of you.

20:04.540 --> 20:06.630
Were you even listening?

20:06.630 --> 20:08.580
I don't know what's happened to you,

20:08.580 --> 20:13.100
but I have no interest in continuing a friendship
with this current sly, petty version of you.

20:13.480 --> 20:16.220
You were an asshole before.

20:16.220 --> 20:17.980
But I didn't hate that.

20:19.450 --> 20:23.130
If you want to be an "ordinary" person,
 go ahead, but leave me out of it.

20:29.670 --> 20:32.750
Man, you're harsh, Kengo.

20:35.100 --> 20:38.460
Sorry, Jogoro, but I'm being honest.

20:41.230 --> 20:43.020
I'll make a bet.

20:43.750 --> 20:45.700
I'm going to call Osanai-san.

20:45.700 --> 20:48.270
If I can get her to back down, great.

20:48.970 --> 20:52.990
If I can't, I'll offer a little bit of wisdom,

20:52.990 --> 20:56.400
and explain why I think she's in danger.

21:23.170 --> 21:25.270
Okay, let's begin.

21:25.990 --> 21:32.350
I suspect this can be resolved 
through a series of deductions.
